                <pb facs="0178" n="166" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg166"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">841D.24/27: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Ireland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gray</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-09-25T12:00:00-04:00">September 25,
                            1940—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>66. Department’s No. 64, September 20, 6 p.m. An additional lot of rifles has
                    been declared surplus and is being sold to the British. It is suggested that the
                    Irish Government may wish to instruct Brennan to discuss this matter further
                    with Lothian and Purvis.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
